## How to read this document

Every figure is labelled. There are no unlabelled estimates — where nobody has published a number, the cell says **`no data`** rather than a plausible guess.

⚠️ **`no data` means "not found", not "does not exist".** The 2026-07-23 fact-check found eight cells marked `no data` whose values were published — several of them on pages this document already cited for other figures. They have been filled in. Treat a remaining `no data` as a prompt to look again, not as proof the measurement was never made.

| Tag | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **M** | Measured by an independent third party |
| **V** | Vendor claim (datasheet, product brief, marketing) — not a measurement |
| **`no data`** | Nothing published. Do not extrapolate. |
| ⚡ | Measured **at the wall** (AC plane — includes adapter loss) |
| ▪ | Measured at the **DC input** (inline meter — excludes adapter loss) |
| 🚩 | **A cheaper option is in stock at another Radxa retailer — buy there instead** |
| ⚑ | A cheaper listing exists at another Radxa retailer but is **sold out** — restock target only |

**The AC/DC distinction matters and the two are not interchangeable.** Geerling and CNX measure at the wall; Bret Weber's `sbc.compare` measures at the DC input with a TC66C. A ~10–20% adapter loss sits between them. For rack/PDU budgeting you want the ⚡ figures. No conversion factor has been applied anywhere in this document.

